    2. Generate a 3x3 binary mask with 3-5 set bits; encode as 6x6 using 2x2 accent blocks
    3. Choose accent color from {2,3,5,6,7,8,9}
    4. Build the 23x23 grid with yellow separators at all 5 positions except the one row and one col crossing the instruction region
    5. Fill the instruction-corner edge row/col entirely with yellow; place the 6x6 instruction block at the offset position
    6. For each of the 32 content cells, generate a random 3x3 blue/empty pattern with blue density ~0.33-0.49
    7. Designate 2-4 random content cells as matching; overwrite their mask-on positions with accent color (output state)
    8. Ensure non-designated cells do NOT have blue at all mask positions (reject or flip one mask-position pixel to empty)
    9. To get input: copy output, replace all accent pixels in content cells with blue
